---
import ToolShell from '../layouts/ToolShell.astro';
---
<ToolShell title="My tools · Qadan" description="A private workspace for my repeatable tools, starting with Cover Studio.">
  <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="intro-copy">
      <h1 id="page-title">My tools<span>.</span></h1>
      <p>A small workspace for the things I make and use repeatedly. Open a tool and get straight to work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tools" aria-labelledby="tools-heading">
    <div class="section-head"><h2 id="tools-heading">Available now</h2><span>Made for phone, tablet, and desktop</span></div>
    <a class="tool" href="/tools/cover-studio/index.html?v=8" aria-label="Open Cover Studio">
      <div class="tool-preview" aria-hidden="true"><div class="preview-top"><span>MAKE</span><strong>MODEL</strong></div><div class="preview-bottom"><span>SPOTTED IN</span><b>CITY, REGION</b><span class="preview-flags"><i></i><i></i></span></div></div>
      <div class="tool-copy"><div class="tool-status"><span class="status-dot"></span> READY TO USE</div><h3>Cover Studio</h3><p>Turn any car photo into a consistent carousel cover. Tap the words to edit, let the photo guide contrast, and add location and plate flags.</p><div class="tool-facts"><span>Photo-aware color</span><span>Inline editing</span><span>PNG export</span></div><span class="tool-action">Open Cover Studio <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10h12m-5-5 5 5-5 5" /></svg></span></div>
    </a>
    <details class="install-help"><summary>Add a tool to your Home Screen</summary><p>On iPhone or iPad, open the tool in Safari, tap Share → Add to Home Screen, and leave “Open as Web App” on. Cover Studio has its own icon and opens directly. The app checks for updates when you return to it.</p></details>
  </section>
  <p class="storage-note">Cover Studio saves its working draft in the browser on each device. Exported PNGs are yours to keep or share.</p>
</ToolShell>
